From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:16:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2775/2775] HID: input: Map Call Mute Toggle to KEY_MICMUTE

Call Mute Toggle (Generic Desktop 0xE1, in a Call State Management
Control collection, HUTRR106) is a one-shot control that toggles the
microphone mute during a call. The Surface Laptop 8 keyboard sends it
from its microphone key, and hid-input does not map it, so the key
does nothing.

Map it to KEY_MICMUTE, as is done for System Microphone Mute and the
Telephony page's Phone Mute.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/hid/hid-input.c | 4 ++++
 include/linux/hid.h     | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-input.c b/drivers/hid/hid-input.c
index edd6bbf..26fe90e 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-input.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-input.c
@@ -975,6 +975,10 @@ static void hidinput_configure_usage(struct hid_input *hidinput, struct hid_fiel
 			}
 			goto unknown;
 
+		case HID_GD_CALL_MUTE_TOGGLE:
+			map_key_clear(KEY_MICMUTE);
+			break;
+
 		default: goto unknown;
 		}
 
diff --git a/include/linux/hid.h b/include/linux/hid.h
index 45f713f..48e761d 100644
--- a/include/linux/hid.h
+++ b/include/linux/hid.h
@@ -226,6 +226,8 @@ struct hid_item {
 #define HID_GD_RFKILL_BTN	0x000100c6
 #define HID_GD_RFKILL_LED	0x000100c7
 #define HID_GD_RFKILL_SWITCH	0x000100c8
+/* Call State Management Control CA usage codes */
+#define HID_GD_CALL_MUTE_TOGGLE	0x000100e1
 
 #define HID_DC_BATTERYSTRENGTH	0x00060020
 
